{
  "enum": "SpellInterruptFlags",
  "description": "What cancels an AURA or a CHANNEL — the enum behind SpellInterrupts.AuraInterruptFlags[2] and SpellInterrupts.ChannelInterruptFlags[2], packed 32 bits per column (bit B lives in column B//32 at 1<<(B%32)). DO NOT CONFUSE IT WITH THE CAST COLUMN: SpellInterrupts.InterruptFlags is a DIFFERENT enum (see spell_interrupts_interrupt_flags.json) where movement is bit 0, and assuming the three columns shared one enum already put two wrong numbers in the feature queue — the channel figure was out by 4.4x. Here movement is bit 3, MovingCancels. `handler` marks the bits the pack ships; adding one is a data edit here plus a pill type. VERIFIED IN GAME on Epsilon (docs/DECISIONS.md, \"EPSILON BEHAVIOUR\"): Kneel 234220 and Sleep 52742 carry bit 3 and both ended the moment the user walked, while Kneel 115368 and Sleep 105595 have no interrupt row and both survived — 4 of 4 clean.",
  "source": [
    "https://wowdev.wiki/EnumeratedString#SpellInterruptFlags",
    "https://wowdev.wiki/DB/SpellInterrupts"
  ],
  "keys": "bit number (not the mask value)",
